==Trivia==
*Welterweight Cat and Ectoweight Cat are based on [[wikia:joe:Joe Yabuki|Joe Yabuki]] from the manga ''[[wikipedia:Ashita no Joe|Ashita no Joe]]''. Ectoweight Cat in particular references Joe's white hair seen in the series' often-parodied [https://web.archive.org/web/20220808143623im_/https://i0.wp.com/white-ash.net/whistle/wp-content/uploads/2018/10/tomorrows-Joe-20-259-Joe-ending-.png?w=534&ssl=1 final panel], last words ("I burned my fire until there was nothing left. All that's left is pure white ash."), and [https://web.archive.org/web/20220731094124/https://white-ash.net/whistle/did-joe-die uncertain fate].
*Heavyweight Cat is a reference to former light-flyweight champion [[wikipedia:Yoko Gushiken|Yoko Gushiken]]. His Japanese description refers to how Gushiken became a television personality following his retirement from boxing.
*Welterweight Cat's design is partially recycled from [[Axe Cat (Normal Cat)|Brave Cat]]'s [[Kumanchu Royale]] counterpart.
*Welterweight Cat's attack resembles [[Kang Roo]]'s.
*Welterweight Cat is among the units that were given [[Multi-Hit]] in [[Version 6.0 Update|Version 6.0]].
*Ectoweight Cat's description is missing the hyphen in "near-death experience".
*In [[Version 8.6 Update|Version 8.6]], there was a [https://youtu.be/m2Kxt_doQQE bug] which would cause Ectoweight Cat to freeze in place on the last frame of his attack animation.

